WEBVTT

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.530
In sickness

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.740
and in health,

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.130
do you promise to love fish and cherish life,

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:53.930
from this day forward 
till death do you part?

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.390
<b>Notification Center</b>

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.390
<b>Today's Schedule
</b>11:00 Stocking up White Sand Dome<b></b>

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.010
I hadn't been to Gama Gama in a while.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.640
Must have been a nice dream.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.730
Yeah!

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.660
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.940
Do you think 
the kijimunaa will appreciate it?

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.750
I hope it comes.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:21.490
Yeah.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.600
Okay, see you there!

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.600
Hey, wait up!

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.060
Stocking up is a race against time.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:28.710
Right!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.530
Let's all hunker down and focus.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.420
Right!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.650
Steady, steady...

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.120
Stop!

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.750
There.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.750
One honeycomb grouper.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.410
One honeycomb grouper.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.980
One blackeye thicklip wrasse.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.510
One blackeye thicklip wrasse.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.340
Okay, you're clear.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.360
Karin-san, are you all right?

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.020
You need a lot of strength 
as an attendant, huh?

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.920
It doesn't take long to get used to it!

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.600
All the animals have been stocked.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.680
Thank you!

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.040
Welcome.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.300
This is your new home.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.890
We have more family now.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.140
Yeah.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.810
I collected some stuff!

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.130
Thanks, Marina-san!

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.410
It was fun.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.540
Okay, let's start pasting it on here.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.910
It's a welcome board!

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.910
Kind of like the one at Gama Gama, huh?

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.690
In fact, a bride and groom asked us for it.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.790
They had their first date 
at Gama Gama Aquarium.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.550
<b>Welcome to Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:25.550
They remember the welcome board, 
so they wanted it to look like that.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.000
And they had no idea that you'd made it?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:28.990
Yeah!

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:31.640
So I feel weirdly special about them.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.530
Hello.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.770
Can we help with anything?

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.080
Really?

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.900
I wouldn't be here 
if I didn't want to be.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.650
Okay, could you draw some animals 
on these cards?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.400
Like this.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:44.890
Huh.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:47.490
You're doing some unique stuff in marketing.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:53.240
Sometimes I'm not sure if this is really 
in the best interest of sea life.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.780
But all you can do is take on what's
in front of you with all your heart, right?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.630
I'll help.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.590
Thank you!

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.540
There we go.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.050
We'll be holding the wedding ceremony 
on the day before opening,

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.620
and then on the day after that,

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:17.310
we're scheduled to open it 
to the general public.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.240
Please and thank you.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.320
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.070
I'll be going now.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:36.770
It's <i>actually</i> an aquarium.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.160
It's at a place called White
Sand Dome, apparently.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:42.380
It said to come dressed 
ready to be barefoot, but...

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.590
What's this?

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:52.930
We asked the newlyweds 
for their guests' best features

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.450
and prepared cards that
are perfect for each of them.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:58.310
<b>The Gourmet of the Sea, 
a Finicky Eater</b>

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:58.310
<b>Dear Hana-chan,
Thanks for coming all the way here.
When we were in grade school, we'd never run out of things to talk about. Though we usually just talked about trivial things (lol) But you tell me exactly what you're thinking when I don't know what to do. And I really respect that as a friend. Please never change and always be the Hana-chan that loves to eat.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.310
"<i>Verconia simplex</i>"?

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.920
"Randalli pistol shrimp"?

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.040
"Pufferfish"?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.810
Sea slugs are very picky eaters.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.720
Pistol shrimp build their own nests 
in a hurry. They're hard-working.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.560
Pufferfish move their mouths a lot.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.650
They're talkative.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.200
I get it.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.780
Please explore the facility 
at your leisure after the ceremony.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:21.960
We hope you enjoy your day.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.820
Did you hear that? I'm a sea slug.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.930
Let's go check them out later.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:29.270
Your idea was a hit, Kukuru-san.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.750
Well, I'd better get going.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:33.640
Okay.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.190
<i>Please welcome the bride and groom.</i>

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.920
Congratulations!

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.380
Wow.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.010
So this is what they meant 
by a barefoot wedding.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.080
This is fun!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.460
The sand's nice and soft.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:10.200
Can you do it just as we practiced?

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:10.960
Okay!

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.050
<i>And now for the wedding ring.</i>

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.530
<i>The ring bearer is Yui-chan, 
the bride and groom's daughter,</i>

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.690
<i>who's dressed in a Cape penguin outfit.</i>

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.430
She's adorable.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.440
Eiji-san, can you hear me?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.510
Yes, standing by.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:30.150
<i>It's time now.</i>

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.850
Roger.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:39.070
We'll be taking photos.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:40.160
Over here, please.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.160
Look, Dad, Mom!

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.920
<i>The fish are celebrating, too.</i>

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.170
Here we go.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.510
<i>We ask the guests to join in 
for the next photo.</i>

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:05.820
<i>We decided to hold our wedding at Tingarla, 
because our daughter loves aquariums.</i>

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:11.690
<i>The penguin costume was made for us 
by the aquarium staff.</i>

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:17.400
<i>Seeing how happy our daughter is, 
I'm very glad we held our wedding here.</i>

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.000
<i>Though our wedding was held on sand,</i>

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:32.410
<i>we hope to build a family together 
with a strong foundation.</i>

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.460
Thank you.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.520
There they are!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.820
Randalli pistol shrimp!

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:47.310
They're so small!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.860
I bet they're wimps.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.050
We're done!

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.190
Not yet.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.000
Now we have to do a teardown.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.070
I'll do my best!

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:00.300
But first, thank you for your work.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.540
And thank you for a fantastic wedding.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.290
Thank you.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.900
Good luck on your opening tomorrow.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:10.760
Thanks!

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.940
Welcome.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.180
Welcome.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:20.470
Welcome.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.740
This way, please.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.930
Welcome to Tingarla!

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.280
One moment, please.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.470
Welcome to Tingarla.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.120
The White Sand Dome opens today.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:29.980
Welcome.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.860
All right, let's make it 
another productive day.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.080
Please and thank you!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.160
Thank you for coming.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:38.750
Hey.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:39.530
What's up?

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.320
Udon-chan. Kai.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.330
You're killing it!

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.630
Thanks.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:47.420
You two must be busy.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.360
Maho-chan, you came, too.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.520
Hello.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.290
Dad's doing a lot better now.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.700
Thank goodness.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.200
I'm not actually that busy.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.400
My training period is almost over, too.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.550
Are you going back to Kamee, then?

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:03.190
That's a secret.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.000
You're busy today, aren't you?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.270
We'll go wander around.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:09.940
Yeah, see you later.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.720
I heard there's a lineup at the door.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.160
White Sand Dome's a huge hit!

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.640
Is Shizu-kun coming, too?

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.350
Yeah.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.950
His grandma's bringing him.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.760
It feels like a festival.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.640
I'm pumped!

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:30.760
This is where the injured and weak fish 
come to rest up for a bit.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:34.030
Yakamashi-san, have you moved into
a higher position than you were at Gama Gama?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:35.210
Shut up.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:38.040
There aren't that many doctors 
that specialize in fish,

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.660
and there aren't that many medicines.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:43.420
So we adjust the dosages 
and give them human medication.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.230
Gramps! Grams!

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.640
Thanks for coming!

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:58.230
We wanted to see Choko 
and the others, too.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.900
Everyone, we're going 
to begin feeding the penguins!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:07.490
Mom!

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:09.490
Here.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:13.370
Fuuka-chan's gotten good, too.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:17.000
You wouldn't believe she's the same girl 
who fell into a tank.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.480
Hey, Gramps...

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:25.380
Were there ever times when you felt
miserable working at Gama Gama?

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.720
Plenty of times.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.510
Really?

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:34.520
Yes. Although looking back now, 
they were all good lessons.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:40.280
There's a lot that 
you don't realize until later.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:44.120
Keep working even when times are tough,

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.480
and there will be times 
when you're rewarded.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.540
Just once in a while.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.350
It's been bugging me.

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:59.160
Gama Gama was all fun.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.800
But Tingarla is nothing like that.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:07.670
I still don't know yet, 
if I should have stayed in marketing.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:15.400
Hey, Gramps, what should I do now?

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:21.820
The answer is already in you, Kukuru.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:28.320
Do yourself the favor of turning 
the path you chose into the correct one.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.440
The future of aquariums is up to you now.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:58.720
Well?

00:13:59.200 --> 00:13:59.860
Yeah.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.660
It's good.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.860
Yeah, it is.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:06.830
When I...

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:12.330
When I first came to Gama Gama, 
I'd just lost my dream.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.000
It didn't matter how pretty the fish were.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.370
I felt like I was drowning 
in the bottom of a dark sea.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.020
Me, too.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:24.410
I felt like that 
when Gama Gama was gone.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.380
But it's not like that now.

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:31.310
The animals and water are all dazzling.

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.960
I feel like I could swim on forever.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:38.120
This is our new start, huh?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.900
I love Tingarla.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.300
Me, too.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:51.980
This place, the people who work here, 
all the things that live here.

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.120
I love aquariums.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.800
I'm going to become a First Penguin.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:22.180
I'll be back all grown up.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.790
Off you go.

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:26.330
I'll be back!

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:40.390
<i>There probably isn't just one answer.</i>

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:48.820
<i>I won't stop, even when I'm troubled.</i>

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.220
<i>We'll have the same dreams</i>

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.180
<i>and seek out the future.</i>

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.870
<i>All we can do is...</i>

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.730
<i>...continue thinking about living creatures.</i>

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.920
<b>The aquatope on white sand</b>

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.730
Aquatope Ready Room.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:21.820
Hello.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.180
This is Misakino.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:24.110
Yes.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:28.600
We sent a facility report yesterday by email.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.900
Misakino-kun looks busy.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.570
She's been given USTD work, 
in addition to her project-planning work.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:37.240
Preparations to receive the trainee team 
when they return soon.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.810
That's amazing.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.440
She does attendant work <i>and</i> marketing work.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:42.330
She might get tapped 
to be the director at some point.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.580
Those conditions apply to me as well.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.170
Hey, Nekton.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:51.310
Yes?

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.090
Where's the annual event plan report?

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:54.650
"Nekton"?

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.480
I'm on it.

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:57.710
The plankton seems to have gained 
the ability to swim.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:00.010
So she's worked her way up just a little.

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:02.100
Maeda Akari-san.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.160
Yes, sir!

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.390
You are assigned to Project PR in marketing.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.230
I'm going to be Kukuru-san's junior?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.610
Yay!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.610
I'm honored!

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.880
Next, Takeshita-sensei...

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:16.600
Yes, sir.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:21.300
I hereby direct you to take maternity leave.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.660
Thank you.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.750
I'll give birth to a healthy baby.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:30.300
A lot of the off-the-shelf stuff 
isn't too usable.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:32.620
So we also make our own 
for the specific spot.

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:33.820
Understood.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.520
What?

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:42.560
I was just surprised 
that you're being an actual chief.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.440
And you aren't complaining about women.

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:46.890
What do you expect? Work is work.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.860
You're such a grown-up now!

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.000
I mean... You're actually
pretty old now, aren't you?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.230
Maybe you skipped being a grown-up 
straight to being elderly.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.800
We're the same age!

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:01.070
Are Shiratama and Choko...

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.300
No doubt.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.800
They're a couple.

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.370
But Choko's a geezer, 
and Shiratama's only two-years old.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:10.060
That's not a big deal in the penguin world.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:13.880
Gay couples, age-gap couples, 
love triangles...

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.920
They specialize in free relationships.

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.510
I had no idea.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.570
I hope you find happiness.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:25.550
Hi!

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:29.000
I'm your new caretaker, Marina!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.810
You can call me "Chief."

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.570
You're all business, aren't you?

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:42.700
I can't wait.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.070
It's been two years, huh?

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.540
Let's hold a "Welcome Home" party!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:47.450
Sounds nice.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.250
Make us something awesome, Chef Tsukimi.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.400
Of course.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.580
I want to hear all their stories.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.760
There's a lot I want 
to talk to them about, too.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.310
I can't wait to see them.

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.600
I wonder how they're doing.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:08.280
I'm excited, too.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:15.610
Sorry, there's somewhere 
I want to drop by first.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.510
I'll see you there.

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:23.860
Thank you.

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:25.430
I'm home, Kukuru.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:28.600
Welcome back, Fuuka.

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:54.940
Hey, Fuuka...

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:55.820
Yeah?

00:22:56.280 --> 00:22:58.940
I never knew your name meant "snow."

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:00.220
Yeah.

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:03.940
"Wind flower" refers to the snow 
that flutters on a sunny day.

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:08.030
Fuuka's a perfect name in Okinawa, though.

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:09.200
Is it?

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:13.450
This island's made of wind, 
flowers, and coral.

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:17.950
Wind, flowers, coral,

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:19.590
and soul.
